/-!
# Very ampleness of invertible modules of large degree on a curve

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] — a proper one-dimensional scheme `X` over a field `k` with
`H⁰(X, 𝒪_X) = k` — assume `X` geometrically integral over `k` of genus `g`. This file proves
[Stacks, Tag 0H2V]: an invertible `𝒪_X`-module `ℒ` with `deg(ℒ) ≥ 2g + 1` is very ample.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.surjective_pullbackSectionTop_subschemeι`:
  surjectivity of `H⁰(X, ℒ) ⟶ H⁰(X, ℒ|_Z)` for `ℒ|_Z = ℒ ⊗ i_* 𝒪_Z` is surjectivity of the
  pullback of global sections `H⁰(X, ℒ) ⟶ H⁰(Z, i^* ℒ)`.
* `CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.surjectsOnDegreeTwo_of_forall_isZero_cohomology_idealTwist` and
  `surjectsOnDegreeTwo_of_forall_surjective_subschemeRestrictionπ`: the hypothesis of
  [Stacks, Tag 0E8T] from `H¹(X, ℐ_Z ℒ) = 0`, resp. from surjectivity onto `H⁰(X, ℒ|_Z)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.surjectsOnDegreeTwo_of_two_mul_genus_add_one_le`:
  for `X` integral and `deg(ℒ) ≥ 2g + 1`, [Stacks, Tag 0E3D] gives the hypothesis of
  [Stacks, Tag 0E8T], over any ground field.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.ofIsPullback`: the situation after extension of
  the ground field, with `invertibleCurveDegree_ofIsPullback` and `isIntegral_ofIsPullback`.
* `CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.isRelativelyVeryAmple_of_two_mul_genus_add_one_le`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0H2V]**, an invertible `𝒪_X`-module of degree at least `2g + 1` is very ample.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H2V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H2V)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E3C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E3C)
